      "text": "1. To maximize the given expression \\(\\dfrac{x^4}{x^8 + 2x^6 - 4x^4 + 8x^2 + 16}\\), we first introduce a substitution:\n   \\[\n   y = x^4\n   \\]\n2. Rewriting \\(x^8 + 2x^6 - 4x^4 + 8x^2 + 16\\) in terms of \\(y\\):\n   \\[\n   y^2 + 2y^3 - 4y^2 + 8y + 16\n   \\]\n3. We find the critical points of \\(y^2 + 2y^3 - 4y^2 + 8y + 16\\) by taking its derivative and setting it to zero:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{d}{dy}(y^2 + 2y^3 - 4y^2 + 8y + 16) = 2y + 6y^2 - 8y + 8 = 0\n   \\]\n4. Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   2y^2 - 2y + 8 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y^2 - y + 4 = 0\n   \\]\n5. The discriminant of the quadratic equation \\(y^2 - y + 4 = 0\\) is:\n   \\[\n   (-1)^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 4 = 1 - 16 = -15\n   \\]\n   Since the discriminant is negative, there are no real solutions for \\(y\\).\n\n6. Given that the original expression involves a positive function, the maximum value must occur at the boundary of the real number domain. We examine the limit as \\(y\\) approaches infinity:\n   \\[\n   \\lim_{y \\to \\infty} \\frac{y^2 + 2y^3 - 4y^2 + 8y + 16}{y^8 + 2y^6 - 4y^4 + 8y^2 + 16}\n   \\]\n7. Factor out the highest power of \\(y\\) in both the numerator and the denominator:\n   \\[\n   \\lim_{y \\to \\infty} \\frac{\\frac{y^2}{y^8} + \\frac{2y^3}{y^8} - \\frac{4y^2}{y^8} + \\frac{8y}{y^8} + \\frac{16}{y^8}}{y^8 + 2y^6 - 4y^4 + 8y^2 + 16}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\lim_{y \\to \\infty} \\frac{\\frac{1}{y^6} + \\frac{2}{y^5} - \\frac{4}{y^6} + \\frac{8}{y^7} + \\frac{16}{y^8}}{1 + \\frac{2}{y^4} - \\frac{4}{y^5} + \\frac{8}{y^6} + \\frac{16}{y^8}}\n   \\]\n8. As \\(y \\to \\infty\\), all terms except the first term in the numerator and the last term in the denominator approach zero:\n   \\[\n   \\lim_{y \\to \\infty} \\frac{\\frac{1}{y^6}}{1} = \\frac{1}{y^6} \\to 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\lim_{y \\to \\infty} \\frac{8}{y^7} = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\lim_{y \\to \\infty} \\frac{16}{y^8} = 0\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the expression simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   \\lim_{y \\to \\infty} \\frac{\\frac{1}{y^6}}{1 + \\frac{2}{y^4} - \\frac{4}{y^5} + \\frac{8}{y^6} + \\frac{16}{y^8}} = \\frac{1}{1} \\times \\frac{1}{1 + 0 - \\frac{0}{y^4} + 0 + 0} = 1\n   \\]\n\nConclusion: The maximum value of the given expression is \\[\\boxed{\\frac{1}{24}}\\].",
